{comment: Verse 1}
[G]When peace like a river [C]at - [D]tendeth [G]my way,
When [Em]sorrows like [A]sea billows [D]roll,
What[G]ever my [C]lot, Thou hast [A]taught me to [D]say,
"It is [G]well, it is [C]well [D]with my [G]soul."

{comment: Chorus}
It is [G]well  (It is [D]well)
With my [D]soul  (With my [G]soul)
It is [C]well, it is [G]well [D]with my [G]soul

{comment: Verse 2}
Though Sa[G]tan should buffet, though [C]trials [D]should [G]come
Let this [Em]blest as[A]surance con[D]trol
That [G]Christ has re[C]garded my [A]helpless es[D]tate
And has [G]shed His own [C]blood [D]for my [G]soul

{comment: Verse 3}
My [G]sin O, the bliss of this glo[C-D]rious   [G]thought
My [Em]sin not in [A]part but the [D]whole
Is [G]nailed to the [C]cross and I [A]bear it no [D]more
Praise the [G]Lord, praise the [C]Lord, [D]O my [G]soul

{comment: Verse 4}
And, [G]Lord haste the day when the [C]faith [D]shall be [G]sight
The clouds [Em]be rolled back [A]as a [D]scroll
The [G]trump shall re[C]sound and the [A]Lord shall de[D]scend
Even [G]so it is [C]well [D]with my [G]soul
